WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.880
My name is Madeleine Månsson
and I'm a dancer and choreographer. 

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.360
And I come from Malmö, Sweden,
from Skånes Dance Theater.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.113
I came across contemporary dance 
in 2012,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.160
through my previous job, actually.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.018
I'm a social worker

00:00:34.018 --> 00:00:39.003
and I had a project where I was working with
young girls and women

00:00:39.003 --> 00:00:41.968
with different disabilities.

00:00:42.593 --> 00:00:48.245
And in 2012 Skånes Dance Theater
wrote me asking:

00:00:50.543 --> 00:00:54.730
"Do you have someone in your group
that would like to try contemporary dance?"

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:58.443
And I said: "Yes, I can pass
this question on and see".

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:03.482
There were two women
that wanted to try

00:01:03.482 --> 00:01:09.183
and I also felt that I needed to be
a role model to the others,

00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:11.303
so, I also stepped in to try.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.682
And it was the first time ever
I tried contemporary dance.

00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:23.707
"Uncharted"

00:01:23.707 --> 00:01:27.197
 is a part of Europe Beyond Access.

00:01:27.197 --> 00:01:31.438
We are going to chose three spots
in Malmö

00:01:31.438 --> 00:01:36.628
and basically going to dig deep
into these spaces

00:01:36.628 --> 00:01:40.512
and create a choreography
with these spaces.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:46.348
So, it will be a challenge of
"who we normally see in these spaces?"

00:01:47.662 --> 00:01:50.987
To challenge unexpected bodies

00:01:50.987 --> 00:01:53.313
in unexpected places.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:58.645
So, it will be three spots and three different
choreographies on these spots.

00:01:58.645 --> 00:02:01.240
 

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.643
It is something special
using your body as a tool in your work,

00:02:08.368 --> 00:02:12.183
also your mind and imagination,
but especially for me,

00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:15.552
it's with my body.
I have always been quite physical,

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:18.170
I have done a lot of sports before,

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:23.353
so, I have always liked to push myself
physically.

00:02:23.353 --> 00:02:27.245
Something I discovered here
in contemporary dance

00:02:29.792 --> 00:02:32.975
is that we also really push our minds
somehow,

00:02:32.975 --> 00:02:35.630
especially in the creative process.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.162
And that is something that I really like:

00:02:38.162 --> 00:02:42.920
to constantly step over
these comfort zones.

00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:49.033
Also, my physical barriers,
so, there are a lot of things

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:53.918
that in an individual personal way,
in dance,

00:02:53.918 --> 00:02:56.003
that makes me grow.

00:02:56.878 --> 00:02:59.162
So, that is why I really love it.

00:02:59.162 --> 00:03:04.160
And obviously also because
there is a lot of meeting with people

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.677
in this work.

